@startuml seq-update
!include _style.iuml
title In-app update: download while running, Restart to update

actor User
participant App
participant UpdateService
participant "IUpdateSource\n(StoreUpdateSource)" as Source
participant "IPackageSwitcher\n(PackageSwitcher)" as Switcher
participant Windows as OS

== Check and download (2 min after start, then every 6 h) ==
UpdateService -> Source : CheckAsync()
Source --> UpdateService : UpdateOffer(2.2.0)
alt staged already (Windows' own updater)
  UpdateService -> Switcher : IsStaged(2.2.0) = true
else silent download allowed
  UpdateService -> Source : DownloadAsync() (stage only, progress)
else Store policy off + admin allows + user opted in
  UpdateService -> Switcher : RegisterRestart("--updated")
  UpdateService -> Source : DownloadDespitePolicyAsync()\n(winget upgrade, msstore)
else automatic Store updates off
  UpdateService --> App : Available + Download
  User -> App : Download
  App -> UpdateService : DownloadAsync(window)
  UpdateService -> Source : RequestDownloadAsync()\n(Store consent dialog)
end
UpdateService --> App : Changed(Ready 2.2.0)
App -> App : notice "Update ready", tray item

== Restart to update (or idle install) ==
User -> App : Restart to update
App -> App : ResolveUnsavedEdits, StopAcceptingWork,\nPersistPendingAsync (saves + backup)
App -> UpdateService : SwitchAsync(idle)
UpdateService -> UpdateService : write update-attempt.json
UpdateService -> Switcher : RegisterRestart("--updated")
UpdateService -> Switcher : StartWatchdog(120 s)\n(one-time scheduled task,\noutside the package)
UpdateService -> Switcher : SwitchAsync()
Switcher -> OS : RegisterPackageByFamilyNameAsync(\nForceTargetApplicationShutdown)
alt switch works
  OS -> App : closes the app, registers 2.2.0
  OS -> App : starts 2.2.0 with "--updated"
  App -> UpdateService : EvaluateStartup(): Succeeded
  App -> User : window + What's new
else switch fails
  OS --> Switcher : error
  Switcher --> UpdateService : reason
  UpdateService --> App : Ready again (2nd failure: manual steps)
  App -> App : hotkey + connector back on, show the reason
end
@enduml
